{
  "id": "COMPOUND:23954 - PROTEIN:5814",
  "verbalization": "Fumiquinazoline B appears to exert its biological effects through a shared target, Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including Diplotrin A and Teyin. These compounds, in turn, direct their activity to VMRC-MELG, suggesting a potential pathway where Fumiquinazoline B may influence VMRC-MELG via a common intermediate. The evidence indicates that Fumiquinazoline B and other compounds with similar targets may modulate VMRC-MELG through a shared mechanism involving Thioredoxin, mitochondrial. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Thioredoxin in mediating the interaction between Fumiquinazoline B and VMRC-MELG, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple compounds with overlapping targets reinforces the likelihood of a broader functional role for VMRC-MELG in the context of these interactions.",
